  "id": "nsw_planning_doc_099",
  "text": "Planning Document: docs/dcps/INNERWEST/leichhardt/Leichhardt DCP 2013 - 12 - Part G Section 1-12 - Amdt 19 - Nov 2023-51-100.pdf\n\nClause G7.5.3 - height_limit (development_control): Development within that part of the site highlighted in red on the view cone on Figure G29: Views is to be limited to a maximum height of RL17.70.\n\nClause G7.6.1 - height_limit (development_control): Development along the Johnston Street frontage is to have a maximum wall height of $7 \\mathsf { m }$ (i.e. two storeys) above footpath level, with the exception of the existing commercial building.\n\nClause G7.6.1 - height_limit (development_control): Development on 170 View Street is to respect the building heights and roof forms of the adjoining View Street properties and is to have a maximum ridge height of RL 14.5.\n\nClause G7.6.1 - height_limit (development_control): Development along the Johnston Street frontage is to have a maximum wall height of 4m and maximum building height of $7 . 5 \\mathsf { m }$ (i.e. two storeys) above Johnston Street, except for the portion of the site adjoining the southern boundary where development is to have a maximum wall height of 4m (i.e. one storey plus attic) above Johnston Street (refer to Figures G37-G39).\n\nClause G7.6.1 - height_limit (development_control): The top of the southern boundary wall adjacent to No. 231 Johnston Street is to be a maximum of RL18.10 to reduce the overshadowing to the rear yard of No. 231 Johnston Street\n\n",
